    "body": "You can use `<input type=\"number\">` , `min`, `max` attributes to restrict range of selections and `placeholder` attribute to notify user that the expected input format is `YYYY`. At `input` event pass the `.value` or `.valueAsNumber` to first parameter of `new Date()`\r\n\r\n```\r\n<input type=\"number\" placeholder=\"YYYY\" min=\"2017\" max=\"2100\">\r\n<script>\r\n  document.querySelector(\"input[type=number]\")\r\n  .oninput = e => console.log(new Date(e.target.valueAsNumber, 0, 1))\r\n</script>\r\n```",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
