    "body": "@guss77 We can set the elements within `ShadowDOM` of `<input =\"date\">` at blink which render `\"mm\"`, `\"dd\"` and `\"/\"` to `display:none` using CSS, though doing so affects the `.value` of the element, that is `.value` is `\"\"` and `.valueAsDate` is `null` and neither `input` nor `change` events are dispatched\r\n\r\n```\r\n  <style>\r\n    input::-webkit-datetime-edit-month-field,\r\n    ::-webkit-datetime-edit-day-field,\r\n    ::-webkit-datetime-edit-text {\r\n      display:none;\r\n    }\r\n  </style>\r\n  <input type=\"date\">\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
